    <header class="page-header">
        <p>Subjective · Personal · Final</p>
        <h1>MY <span>RANKINGS</span></h1>
        <span class="subtitle">5 anime. Ranked by gut feeling, rewatchability, and emotional damage.</span>
    </header>

    <section class="rankings-sec">

        <article class="rank-card">
            <b class="rank-num">01</b>
            <div class="rank-info">
                <h2 class="rank-title">Attack on Titan</h2>
                <ul class="rank-tags">
                    <li><span class="tag season">4 Seasons</span></li>
                    <li><span class="tag complete">Complete</span></li>
                    <li><span class="tag">Dark Fantasy</span></li>
                    <li><span class="tag">Action</span></li>
                </ul>
                <p class="rank-desc">
                    Nothing has ever hit me like AoT has. The worlbuilding, the moral ambihuity, all work together to
                    create a masterclass in longform storytelling. Eren's arc alone is one of the most complex character
                    journeys in anime history.
                </p>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="rank-card">
            <b class="rank-num">02</b>
            <div class="rank-info">
                <h2 class="rank-title">Death Note</h2>
                <ul class="rank-tags">
                    <li><span class="tag complete">1 Season</span></li>
                    <li><span class="tag">Psychological</span></li>
                    <li><span class="tag">Thriller</span></li>
                </ul>
                <p class="rank-desc">
                    The anime that introduced so many people to the medium — myself included. The cat-and-mouse between
                    Light and L is relentless. Every episode feels like a chess match. Light Yagami remains one of the
                    most compelling anti-heroes ever written.

                </p>
            </div>
        </article>
        <article class="rank-card">
            <b class="rank-num">03</b>
            <div class="rank-info">
                <h2 class="rank-title">Jujutsu Kaisen</h2>
                <ul class="rank-tags">
                    <li><span class="tag season">2 Seasons</span></li>
                    <li><span class="tag">Supernatural</span></li>
                    <li><span class="tag">Action</span></li>
                </ul>
                <p class="rank-desc">
                    JJK is pure adrenaline. The fight choreography is some of the best in modern anime — MAPPA went
                    absolutely insane with the animation budget. Season 2's Shibuya arc is a jaw-dropping, brutal
                    spectacle that broke social media.
                </p>
            </div>
        </article>
        <article class="rank-card">
            <b class="rank-num">04</b>
            <div class="rank-info">
                <h2 class="rank-title">Death Parade</h2>
                <ul class="rank-tags">
                    <li><span class="tag season">1 Seasons</span></li>
                    <li><span class="tag complete">Complete</span></li>
                    <li><span class="tag">Psychological</span></li>
                    <li><span class="tag">Drama</span></li>
                </ul>
                <p class="rank-desc">
                    Criminally underrated. 12 episodes and it hits harder than most 50-episode series. The concept —
                    dead souls playing bar games to determine their fate — is deceptively simple but philosophically
                    deep. If you haven't watched this, stop what you're doing.
                </p>
            </div>
        </article>
        <article class="rank-card">
            <b class="rank-num">05</b>
            <div class="rank-info">
                <h2 class="rank-title">Assassination Classroom</h2>
                <ul class="rank-tags">
                    <li><span class="tag season">2 Seasons</span></li>
                    <li><span class="tag complete">Complete</span></li>
                    <li><span class="tag">Comedy</span></li>
                    <li><span class="tag">Action</span></li>
                </ul>
                <p class="rank-desc">
                    On the surface it sounds ridiculous — a class of students trying to assassinate their alien teacher.
                    But Koro-sensei is one of the most wholesome, emotionally rich characters in anime. The final arc
                    genuinely made me cry. A perfect ending too — which is rare.

                </p>
            </div>
        </article>
    </section>

